NOTES={
1669:('The speaker wonders what a purser ought to do during naval combat.','What should a purser do in a sea battle...? keeps the role-specific uncertainty, naval-combat setting and unfinished question. Purser translates the explicit 主計長 role; it does not invent a rank or make the speaker useless during ordinary sailing.'),
1670:('The speaker tentatively considers working on the financial report while time is available.','I might as well work on the financial report while I have the chance... preserves the personal tentative intention and available opportunity. 決算報告書 supports financial report; no monthly or annual period is specified here. The complete three-row thought must remain visible.'),
1671:('The speaker reflects that a purser is idle during a naval battle.','A purser has nothing to do in a sea battle... preserves the limited battle situation and mild dissatisfaction. Ordinary1459-1470 show active finance duties while sailing; the line does not deny the role a use at sea generally.'),
1672:('The speaker wishes they could haggle while fighting.','I wish I could haggle and fight at the same time... keeps the fanciful simultaneous actions and wistful hypothetical. It does not claim combat bargaining is possible, add a merchant opponent or imply a purchase or surrender negotiation.'),
1673:('The rougher voice observes that one cannot haggle in naval combat and seeks agreement.','You can\'t haggle in a sea battle, can you...? retains the reflective question, battle-only scope and colloquial voice without invented profanity. It does not generalize the restriction to peaceful ports or normal sailing.'),
1674:('The older voice starts thinking about this month\'s profits, then reacts in surprise to a roaring noise.','This month\'s profits... Whoa! What\'s that racket?! preserves the explicit month, interrupted thought and startled question. Racket naturally conveys the loud battle noise without identifying a specific gun, damage amount, ship or profit figure.'),
1675:('The simple voice says they also want to fight but leaves the thought unfinished.','I want to fight, too... preserves おいら, the inclusive too and hesitant trailing wish. It keeps the simple voice without caricature and does not turn desire into an order, permission, earned assignment or completed participation. Initial ASCII I is required.'),
1676:('The measured voice says they cannot play much of an active part from here during naval combat.','I can\'t do much here during a sea battle is natural restrained speech for 活躍できませんな. It retains the location and combat scope rather than declaring total incompetence or inability to serve while sailing. Initial I must survive.'),
1677:('Rafael reflects that the purser role is powerless in battle.','A purser is helpless in battle... preserves his discouraged assessment and explicit combat context. This is a character\'s role-specific reflection, not an engine guarantee that the individual cannot fight from any assignment.'),
1678:('Hodram forcefully says this is no time to calculate profits.','No time to calculate profits! is a natural urgent exclamation with the situation supplying the omitted subject. It retains calculation and priority without changing money or implying a completed financial loss. The existing Hodram Joakim Bergstrom metadata correctly identifies genuine captain1.'),
1679:('Lil exasperatedly asks what she is supposed to do in the Purser\'s Office.','What am I supposed to do in the Purser\'s Office?! preserves her personal complaint, rhetorical question and explicit room. The room label matches established crew-help terminology; no reassignment, insult to a named officer or new rank is added.'),
1680:('Maria says that from here she cannot give everyone directions.','I can\'t give the crew orders from here! preserves the personal frustration and location-dependent command limitation. The crew is the contextual referent of 皆 in this shipboard battle role; it does not establish universal inability to command or imply that an order was actually issued.'),
}
